\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For $n\geq 3$ and positive capacities $R,R_{1},\dots ,R_k$, do neighborhood-defined symplectic embeddings of the disjoint closed standard 2n-balls of capacities $R_i$ into the interior of the standard ball of capacity R exist exactly when $\Sigma _i$ $R_i^{n}<R^{n}$ and $R_i+R_j<R$ for every distinct pair i,j? Capacity is $\pi $ times squared Euclidean radius.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For $n\geq 3$ and positive capacities $R,R_{1},\dots ,R_k$, do neighborhood-defined symplectic embeddings of the disjoint closed standard 2n-balls of capacities $R_i$ into the interior of the standard ball of capacity R exist exactly when $\Sigma _i$ $R_i^{n}<R^{n}$ and $R_i+R_j<R$ for every distinct pair i,j? Capacity is $\pi $ times squared Euclidean radius.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Symplectic-Ball-Packings-in-Higher-Dimensions-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

